From: ClauCoDillo NuttX port
Subject: [PATCH] mwin: fix WM_CHAR generation for unmapped keys

MwDeliverKbdEvent() (src/mwin/winevent.c) sets VK_Code to VK_NONAME for
any MWKEY that doesn't match one of the named special-key cases in its
switch statement -- which is every ordinary printable character (a-z,
0-9, punctuation, space), since none of those have their own case.

VK_NONAME is 0xFC, not -1. The code right after the switch treats
"VK_Code != -1" as "this is a real, known VK code" and sets bit 24 of
lParam to say so:

    if (VK_Code == -1)
        VK_Code = keyvalue;
    else
        lParam |= (1 << 24);

TranslateMessage() (src/mwin/winuser.c) only turns a WM_KEYDOWN into a
WM_CHAR when that same bit is clear:

    if (lpMsg->message == WM_KEYDOWN &&
        (!(lpMsg->lParam & (1<<24)) || bAltStatus)) {
        PostMessage(lpMsg->hwnd, WM_CHAR, ...);
    }

So every ordinary character key -- landing in the switch's default
case, getting VK_NONAME, getting bit 24 set -- never produces a
WM_CHAR. An application only ever sees WM_KEYDOWN/WM_KEYUP with
wParam==VK_NONAME for a-z/0-9/space/etc., with no way to recover which
character was actually typed. Real text entry (an Fl_Input-equivalent,
a text field, anything that types by character rather than by
special-function key) cannot work through this API as a result.

Fix: don't assign VK_NONAME in the default case. Leave VK_Code at its
initial -1, so the "no VK defined" branch handles it correctly and
WM_CHAR gets generated the same way it already does for X11's other,
recognized special keys.

Found and verified while porting cFLTK's NuttX/Microwindows-mwin
backend for the ClauCoDillo browser port: this was the last of three
compounding bugs (the other two: a NuttX sim event-loop scheduling gap
that never delivered keyboard events at all for keyboard-only sim
configs, and a missing SetFocus() call in the cFLTK backend itself)
blocking keyboard input end-to-end. Confirmed fixed by typing into a
real cFLTK Fl_Input and seeing the correct characters appear.
---
--- a/src/mwin/winevent.c
+++ b/src/mwin/winevent.c
@@ -451,7 +451,6 @@
 	case MWKEY_LAST:
 #endif
 	default:
-		VK_Code = VK_NONAME;
 		break;
 	}

